{"assets":["/statement-assets/884c49190ae5c9d1fa5a9a9e255e5f3f418122cf6d8346fd1d40dd6380e56565.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"434","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Furukawa Nagisa's Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day, Okazaki Tomoya has bought a tree for Furukawa Nagisa's birthday. The tree is so strange that every node of the tree has a value. The value of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th node is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Now Furukawa Nagisa and Okazaki Tomoya want to play a game on the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(s, e)"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the path from node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" to node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"e"},{"kind":"text","text":", we can write down the sequence of the values of nodes on path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(s, e)"},{"kind":"text","text":", and denote this sequence as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S(s, e)"},{"kind":"text","text":". We define the value of the sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G(S(s, e))"},{"kind":"text","text":" as follows. Suppose that the sequence is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z0, z1...zl - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the length of the sequence. We define "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"G(S(s, e)) = z0 × k0 + z1 × k1 + ... + zl - 1 × kl - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(s, e)"},{"kind":"text","text":" satisfies "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/884c49190ae5c9d1fa5a9a9e255e5f3f418122cf6d8346fd1d40dd6380e56565.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(s, e)"},{"kind":"text","text":" belongs to Furukawa Nagisa, otherwise it belongs to Okazaki Tomoya."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Calculating who has more paths is too easy, so they want to play something more difficult. Furukawa Nagisa thinks that if paths "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, p2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p2, p3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" belong to her, then path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, p3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" belongs to her as well. Also, she thinks that if paths "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, p2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p2, p3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" belong to Okazaki Tomoya, then path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, p3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" belongs to Okazaki Tomoya as well. But in fact, this conclusion isn't always right. So now Furukawa Nagisa wants to know how many triplets "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, p2, p3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" are correct for the conclusion, and this is your task."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x (1 ≤ n ≤ 105; 2 ≤ y ≤ 109; 1 ≤ k < y; 0 ≤ x < y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" being the number of nodes on the tree. It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a prime number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th integer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi (0 ≤ vi < y)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then follow "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines, each line contains two integers, denoting an edge of the tree. The nodes of the tree are numbered from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the number of triplets that are correct for Furukawa Nagisa's conclusion."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2 1 0\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 5 2 1\n4 3 1\n1 2\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"14\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 13 8 12\n0 12 7 4 12 0 8 12\n1 8\n8 4\n4 6\n6 2\n2 3\n8 5\n2 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"341\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"434E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/434/problem/E"}